---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
import joyImage from '../assets/people/joy-professional-wide.jpg';
import textureImage from '../assets/services/body-soul-spirit-texture.jpg';
import { organizationSchema, serviceSchema } from '../data/schema';
---
<BaseLayout title="Team Coaching & Workshops | Threads Coaching" description="Team coaching and workshops that build reflective practice, stronger connection and values-led work." path="/team-workshops" schema={[organizationSchema, serviceSchema('Team coaching and workshops', '/team-workshops', 'Team coaching and workshops for reflective practice, stronger connection and values-led work.')] }>
  <section class="hero-copy section team-hero"><span class="team-hero__loop team-hero__loop--one" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="team-hero__loop team-hero__loop--two" aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="container"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Teams and workshops' }]} /><div class="split split--media team-hero__grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">For teams and organisations</p><h1>Turn your ethos into the way your team actually works.</h1><p class="lead">Healthy culture takes more than a mission statement. We help teams clarify what they value, understand how people contribute and create practices that support both effectiveness and wellbeing.</p><a class="button button--primary" href="/contact">Talk to us about your team</a></div><div class="team-hero__visual"><div class="team-hero__texture" aria-hidden="true"><Image src={textureImage} alt="" width={300} quality={32} loading="eager" /></div><Image src={joyImage} alt="Joy Blundell of Threads Coaching" width={640} densities={[1, 1.5]} sizes="(min-width: 64rem) 40vw, 88vw" quality={58} /><span class="team-hero__shape" aria-hidden="true"></span></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section section--tint"><div class="container narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Who this is for</p><h2>Good teams still need space to pause and reflect.</h2><p>This work is for teams and organisations that want to bring shared values, people’s strengths and day-to-day practice closer together—particularly where the work carries professional and human complexity.</p><p>Threads Coaching brings experience across church, public and third-sector contexts, including health, social care and pastoral settings.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Ways to work together</p><h2>Start with the conversation your team needs.</h2></div><p class="lead">Joy and Paul will use your context and hoped-for change to shape an appropriate workshop or coaching approach.</p></div><div class="card-grid team-offers"><article class="card"><h3>Group and team coaching</h3><p>Reflective practice and deeper connection for teams working with professional and human complexity.</p><p class="card-note">Create space to notice what is happening and decide how you want to work together.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Discover your team’s Working Genius</h3><p>Explore the Working Genius framework and identify how different strengths can contribute more effectively across the life of your team.</p><p class="card-note">Build shared language around the ways people contribute.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Organisational values curation</h3><p>Clarify the values that genuinely guide your team, then bridge the gap between what you say matters and how you lead, decide and work together.</p><p class="card-note">Connect stated values with practical decisions and habits.</p></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="section section--plan"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">What happens next</p><h2>A simple commissioning process</h2><ol class="steps"><li><strong>Clarify the need.</strong><span>Talk through your context, team and the change you hope to make.</span></li><li><strong>Shape the session.</strong><span>Agree a focused, appropriate workshop or coaching approach and the practical requirements to clarify together.</span></li><li><strong>Carry learning into practice.</strong><span>Leave with shared language and useful next steps for your team to take forward.</span></li></ol></div></section>
  <section class="section team-proof"><span class="team-proof__thread" aria-hidden="true">together</span><div class="container narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Who delivers it</p><h2>Facilitation shaped by coaching, leadership and pastoral experience.</h2><p>Joy and Paul are the people behind Threads Coaching. Joy is a qualified Life and Leadership Coach, pastor, organisational leader and speaker; Paul is a pastor and coach currently training in Breakthrough Life Coaching. <a href="/about">Read more about their approaches</a>.</p><p>They do not begin with a generic team formula. The first conversation is there to understand your setting, the people involved and the outcome you are hoping for.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section section--tint"><div class="container narrow"><h2>Questions to explore together</h2><details><summary>Can a workshop be tailored to our team?</summary><p>Yes. The starting point is your context and the change your team hopes to make; you will clarify an appropriate approach and practical requirements together.</p></details><details><summary>Is this only for church teams?</summary><p>No. The existing offer includes experience relevant to public, third-sector, health, social care and pastoral settings.</p></details><details><summary>What will we clarify before we begin?</summary><p>We will talk through your team, the issue or opportunity you want to address, the hoped-for outcome and which of the available approaches is the most useful fit.</p></details><details><summary>Can this replace specialist organisational or clinical support?</summary><p>No. This is coaching and facilitated workshop work. Where a team needs specialist professional support, the first conversation can help clarify whether this offer is appropriate.</p></details></div></section>
  <CallToAction title="Give your team space to work more thoughtfully together." body="Start with a conversation about what your team needs." primaryHref="/contact" primaryLabel="Talk to us about your team" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .team-hero { isolation: isolate; }
  .team-hero__grid { align-items: center; }
  .team-hero__visual { position: relative; z-index: 1; min-height: 20rem; padding: 1rem 1.5rem 1rem 0; }
  .team-hero__visual > :global(img) { position: relative; z-index: 2; display: block; width: min(100%, 31rem); margin-right: auto; aspect-ratio: 0.95; object-fit: cover; object-position: 50% 42%; border-radius: 36% 64% 18% 49% / 47% 41% 22% 53%; }
  .team-hero__texture { position: absolute; z-index: 1; right: 0; bottom: -0.5rem; width: 49%; height: 64%; overflow: hidden; border-radius: 58% 42% 48% 52%; opacity: 0.55; transform: rotate(10deg); }
  .team-hero__texture :global(img) { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  .team-hero__shape { position: absolute; z-index: 3; top: 0; right: 0.5rem; width: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5rem); aspect-ratio: 1; background: var(--color-coral); border-radius: 61% 39% 44% 56%; transform: rotate(-18deg); }
  .team-hero__loop { position: absolute; z-index: 0; width: 34rem; height: 8rem; border: 2px solid rgb(47 127 141 / 0.18); border-radius: 50%; }
  .team-hero__loop--one { top: 5rem; right: -10rem; transform: rotate(-12deg); }
  .team-hero__loop--two { right: -8rem; bottom: 2rem; transform: rotate(9deg); }
  .team-offers .card { display: grid; align-content: start; gap: var(--space-4); }
  .team-offers .card > * { margin: 0; }
  .card-note { padding-top: var(--space-4); border-top: 1px solid rgb(23 56 60 / 0.14); color: var(--color-muted); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
  .team-proof { position: relative; overflow: hidden; background: var(--color-ink); color: var(--color-white); }
  .team-proof h2 { color: inherit; }
  .team-proof .eyebrow { color: #b7dcdf; }
  .team-proof p { color: #d6e6e7; }
  .team-proof a { color: var(--color-sand); }
  .team-proof__thread { position: absolute; right: -3rem; bottom: -4rem; color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.04); font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: clamp(7rem, 21vw, 16rem); font-style: italic; transform: rotate(-9deg); }
</style>
